---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Icon from "../../components/Icon.astro";

const title = "Airtel WiFi not working? Fixes for Xstream Fiber";
const description = "Airtel WiFi connected but no internet? Step by step fixes for Xstream Fiber and Airtel broadband, plus a one click Chrome option.";

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://arverma.dev/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Guides", item: "https://arverma.dev/guides/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Airtel WiFi not working", item: "https://arverma.dev/guides/airtel-wifi-not-working/" },
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="section guide-page">
    <p class="section-label"><Icon name="book-open" size={14} />Guide</p>
    <h1 class="guide-title">Airtel WiFi not working? Fixes for Xstream Fiber</h1>
    
    <div class="guide-content">
      <p class="guide-lead">
        Your Airtel Xstream Fiber WiFi shows connected, but nothing loads. This happens when the connection goes idle, 
        the router loses sync with the network, or there is a fiber link issue. Here is what to check, in order.
      </p>

      <h2 class="guide-h2"><Icon name="activity" size={16} />Check the LOS light</h2>
      <p>
        Look at the lights on your Airtel router. The most important one is labeled LOS (Loss of Signal) or PON. 
        If this light is red or blinking, the fiber cable is disconnected or damaged.
      </p>
      <p>
        Check the fiber cable at the back of the router. It should be firmly plugged in. If it is loose, push it in 
        until you hear a click. Also check where the fiber cable enters your home. If everything looks fine but the 
        LOS light is still red, call Airtel support.
      </p>

      <h2 class="guide-h2"><Icon name="smartphone" size={16} />Check plan and balance in Airtel Thanks</h2>
      <p>
        Open the Airtel Thanks app. Go to your Xstream Fiber connection and check the plan status. If your plan has 
        expired or your bill is overdue, the internet will not work even if WiFi is connected.
      </p>
      <p>
        Pay the bill or recharge if needed. It can take 5 to 10 minutes for the connection to come back after payment.
      </p>

      <h2 class="guide-h2"><Icon name="refresh-cw" size={16} />Restart order</h2>
      <p>
        Turn off the router. Wait 30 seconds. Turn it back on and wait 2 minutes for all lights to stabilize. 
        This clears the connection state and forces the router to get a fresh link from Airtel.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you have a separate ONT (the small box where the fiber cable comes in), restart that first, wait 30 seconds, 
        then restart the router.
      </p>

      <h2 class="guide-h2"><Icon name="settings" size={16} />Router admin page (192.168.1.1)</h2>
      <p>
        Open a browser and go to <a href="http://192.168.1.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">192.168.1.1<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span></a>. 
        This is the router admin page. The default username is usually <code>admin</code> and the password is on 
        the sticker on the router.
      </p>
      <p>
        Check the WAN or Internet status. If it says disconnected, the router is not getting an IP from Airtel. 
        Restart the router and wait 2 minutes. If it still says disconnected, call Airtel support.
      </p>

      <h2 class="guide-h2"><Icon name="zap" size={16} />Stuck connection and WiFi Hammer</h2>
      <p>
        Sometimes the router goes idle and does not wake up when you try to load a page. Airtel Xstream Fiber routers 
        do this less often than Jio, but it still happens.
      </p>
      <p>
        I built <a href="/projects/wifi-hammer/">WiFi Hammer</a> to fix this. It is a Chrome extension that wakes 
        the connection with one click. You can also turn on Auto-hammer to keep the connection fresh every 30 minutes. 
        It works by sending a small network request that forces the router to reset the link.
      </p>
      <p>
        WiFi Hammer does not make your internet faster or increase your plan speed. It only wakes a stuck connection.
      </p>

      <h2 class="guide-h2"><Icon name="phone" size={16} />Airtel support</h2>
      <p>
        If none of the above work, contact Airtel support:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Call <strong>121</strong> from your Airtel mobile number, or <strong>1800-103-4444</strong> from any phone.</li>
        <li>Use the Airtel Thanks app: Go to Help > Chat with us.</li>
        <li>Visit the <a href="https://www.airtel.in/broadband/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Airtel Broadband Help Center<span class="sr-only"> (opens in new tab)</span></a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        When you call, tell them your router lights are on but you cannot load any pages. They can reset your connection 
        from their side or schedule a technician visit.
      </p>

      <h2 class="guide-h2"><Icon name="help-circle" size={16} />FAQ</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-q">Why does my Airtel WiFi say connected but nothing loads?</h3>
          <p class="faq-a">
            This usually happens when the router goes idle, the fiber link is down, or your plan has expired. 
            Check the LOS light on the router. If it is red, the fiber cable is disconnected.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-q">What does the LOS light mean on my Airtel router?</h3>
          <p class="faq-a">
            LOS stands for Loss of Signal. If the LOS light is red or blinking, the fiber cable is disconnected 
            or damaged. Check the cable at the back of the router and where it enters your home.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-q">How do I check my Airtel Xstream Fiber plan status?</h3>
          <p class="faq-a">
            Open the Airtel Thanks app, go to your Xstream Fiber connection, and check the plan details. 
            If your bill is overdue or your plan has expired, pay or recharge in the app.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-q">What is the difference between Airtel Xstream Fiber and V-Fiber?</h3>
          <p class="faq-a">
            Xstream Fiber is the current branding for Airtel's fiber broadband service. V-Fiber was the old name. 
            They are the same product. If you have V-Fiber, these steps still apply.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-q">Will WiFi Hammer work with Airtel Xstream Fiber?</h3>
          <p class="faq-a">
            Yes. WiFi Hammer works with any broadband or router, including Airtel Xstream Fiber. It wakes a stuck 
            connection when pages will not load even though WiFi says connected.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="guide-related">
        <h3 class="guide-related-title">Related guides</h3>
        <ul class="guide-related-list">
          <li><a href="/guides/wifi-connected-no-internet/"><Icon name="arrow-right" size={14} />WiFi connected but no internet: 8 fixes that work</a></li>
          <li><a href="/guides/jio-wifi-not-working/"><Icon name="arrow-right" size={14} />Jio WiFi not working? Fixes for JioFiber and AirFiber</a></li>
          <li><a href="/projects/wifi-hammer/"><Icon name="arrow-right" size={14} />WiFi Hammer Chrome extension</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .guide-page {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .guide-title {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1.5rem 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .guide-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .guide-lead {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .guide-content p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .guide-content ul {
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .guide-content li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .guide-content code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--surface);
    padding: 0.125rem 0.375rem;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
  }

  .guide-content a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .guide-content a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-2);
  }

  .guide-h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .faq-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .faq-item {
    padding: 1rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
  }

  .faq-q {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .faq-a {
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .guide-related {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
  }

  .guide-related-title {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .guide-related-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .guide-related-list a {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .guide-related-list a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .guide-title {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
